Integration 1, AutoStash 409 and Unit 605 passed, zero failures/skips/exclusions. All hosts ran sequentially; the dedicated integration host exited before fresh focused and Unit hosts. The final current rebuild emitted the same 7 existing production and 27 test warnings; subsequent incremental runs emitted none. Earlier validation passed 408/604 before the additional direct-only capacity test; the final rebuilt sequence includes it. Fresh installed API/Lib/SurvivalMod/Essentials assembly versions are all 1.22.7.0; API file version 1.22.0, others 1.22.7. No game/client/server launch, tooling installation or standalone audit/verification/log files occurred.

Independent completion audit by audit directly consulted the skill, full current plan/proposal, new assessment implementation and owner diffs, existing/new assertion sensitivity, documentation mapping and final rebuilt evidence. Verdict: P5.1–P5.6 and completion fully satisfied, no confirmed implementation/documentation issues or evidence gaps. Markers were checked only after the second review and this verdict. Automated evidence does not establish live-game acceptance.

## Phase 6: Remove migration scaffolding and verify acceptance

Outcome: The proposed boundaries are the sole implementation, with the established behavior preserved.
Dependencies: Phases 1–5.
Sources: Proposal Source layout and dependencies, Validation requirements, Relationship to alloy deposits, Acceptance criteria and Evidence limits.

☐ P6.1 Remove obsolete transfer loops, predicates/session flags/finalizer plumbing and temporary migration facades after all consumers/tests migrate. Retain only explicitly documented compatibility boundaries, including the resolved preferred-slot decision.
☐ P6.2 Audit dependencies: planning depends on policy/engine inventory contracts; executor on engine/move contracts; adapters on owning target APIs; service on these boundaries; interaction/network roots contain no transfer loops. One file owns each responsibility; no general inventory framework or alloy path changes.
☐ P6.3 Map each proposal requirement to final source/tests and inspect regression sensitivity. Preserve all established scenario outcomes, engine restrictions, exact quantity/identity/attributes, unrelated slots, durable persistence, finite attempts and cleanup effects; test-count growth is not acceptance.
☐ P6.4 Run final separate Integration, focused AutoStash and repository Unit suites through subagents with fresh unit hosts after integration. Record revision, exact commands, pass/fail/skip counts, assembly metadata and warnings here; no exclusions or silent skips.
☐ P6.5 Perform a second source/plan/proposal review and obtain an independent final audit of preserved behavior, adapter ownership, planner progress, assessment purity, real Harmony dispatch and production scope. Resolve every required finding before completion.
☐ P6.6 Update proposal status to implemented only after source and final evidence satisfy it; identify automated versus user-run live evidence accurately. No game launch is required or authorized by this plan.
☐ Final acceptance: All targets share the concrete executor and coordinator; policies own live routing/limits/order, adapters own lifecycle/persistence, assessment expresses certainty, engine algorithms remain authoritative, old active implementations are removed, and all required regressions/reviews/audits pass without a gameplay change.
